{
  "slug": "css_image_transparency",
  "course": "css",
  "order": 87,
  "url": "/css/css_image_transparency.asp",
  "title": "CSS Opacity",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "CSS Opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Image Opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The opacity property specifies the opacity/transparency of an element."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The opacity property can take a value from 0.0 - 1.0:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "0.0 - The element will be completely transparent",
        "0.5 - The element will be 50% transparent",
        "1.0 - Default. The element will be fully opaque"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_forest.jpg",
      "alt": "Forest"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 0.2"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_forest.jpg",
      "alt": "Forest"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 0.5"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_forest.jpg",
      "alt": "Forest"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 1.0(default)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "img {\n  opacity: 0.5;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_image_opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Opacity and :hover"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The opacity property is often used with\n\n:hover\nto change the opacity on mouse-over:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_lights.jpg",
      "alt": "Northern Lights"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_mountains.jpg",
      "alt": "Mountains"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_5terre.jpg",
      "alt": "Italy"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "img {\n  opacity: 0.5;\n}\n\nimg:hover {\n  opacity: 1.0;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_image_transparency"
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Reversed Hover Effect"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Here is an example of reversed hover effect:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_lights.jpg",
      "alt": "Northern Lights"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_mountains.jpg",
      "alt": "Mountains"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_5terre.jpg",
      "alt": "Italy"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "img:hover {\n  opacity: 0.5;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_image_transparency2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Transparent Boxes"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When using the\nopacity property to add transparency to the background of an element, all child elements\ninherit the same transparency. This can make the text inside a transparent element hard to read:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 0.6"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 0.3"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "opacity 0.1"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "div {\n  opacity: 0.3;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_opacity_box"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Transparency using background-color"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "To NOT apply the transparency to child elements, you can use the\nbackground-color property\nwith an RGBA value."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "RGBA color values are an extension of RGB color values with an alpha channel\n- which specifies the opacity for a color."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "An RGBA color value is specified with: rgba(red, green, blue, alpha). Where\nthe alpha parameter is a number between 0.0 (fully transparent) and 1.0 (fully\nopaque)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: You will learn more about RGBA Colors in our CSS Colors Chapter."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The following example sets the opacity for the background color and not the text:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "100% opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "60% opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "30% opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "10% opacity"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "div {\n  background: rgba(4, 170, 109, 0.3) /* Green background with 30%\nopacity */\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_opacity_box2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Text in Transparent Box"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This is some text that is placed in the transparent box."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<html>\n\n<head>\n\n<style>\n\ndiv.background {\n\n    background: url(klematis.jpg) repeat;\n\n    border: 2px solid black;\n\n}\n\ndiv.transbox {\n\n    margin: 30px;\n\n    background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);\n\n    border: 1px solid black;\n\n}\n\ndiv.transbox p {\n\n  margin: 5%;\n\n  font-weight: bold;\n\n    color: #000000;\n\n}\n\n</style>\n\n</head>\n\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"background\">\n\n  <div class=\"transbox\">\n\n    <p>This is some text that is placed in the transparent box.</p>\n\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_transparency"
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Example explained"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Create a <div> element (class=\"background\") with a background image, and a border.",
        "Create another <div> (class=\"transbox\") inside the first <div>.",
        "The\n<div class=\"transbox\"> have a 0.6 transparent background color, and a border.",
        "Inside the transparent\n<div>, we add some text inside a <p> element."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Property"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Property", "Description"],
      "rows": [["opacity", "Sets the opacity level for an element"]]
    }
  ]
}
